-- Target compiler: main (build 1.6.112).  Answers: MAYBE BOOLEAN; JUST TRUE is the text's yes, NOTHING means
-- the text does not answer (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled).
--
-- Article 1(1) and (2) state the subject-matter and the objectives of the Regulation and create no rule:
-- they are `inert` for reason (1) (not operative: a purpose or objects clause).  Article 1(3) is a flat
-- negative ("shall be neither restricted nor prohibited") and is encoded.
-- ============================================================================

§ `Chapter I heading and Article 1(1) and (2): subject-matter and objectives (inert, reason 1: not operative)`

-- src:12 | CHAPTER I
-- src:13 | General provisions
-- src:14 | Article 1
-- src:15 | Subject-matter and objectives
-- src:16 | 1. This Regulation lays down rules relating to the protection of natural persons with regard to the processing of personal data and rules relating to the free movement of personal data.
-- src:17 | 2. This Regulation protects fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons and in particular their right to the protection of personal data.
-- INERT (reason 1, not operative: titles, headings, and a purpose or objects clause that creates no rule).
-- Article 1(1) says what the rules of the Regulation are about; Article 1(2) says what the Regulation protects.
-- Neither says what a person must, may or may not do.  Both are read as aids to understanding the other
-- provisions and are not encoded (NOTES: Coverage table; a lawyer may wish to ask whether Art 1(2) should
-- weigh in an open-textured judgment of a later part: Open questions).

§ `Article 1(3): the free movement of personal data within the Union is not to be restricted or prohibited for data protection reasons`

-- src:18 | 3. The free movement of personal data within the Union shall be neither restricted nor prohibited for reasons connected with the protection of natural persons with regard to the processing of personal data.
@ref Art 1(3) free movement of personal data (src:18)
GIVEN `the personal data move within the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure restricts or prohibits that movement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason for the measure is connected with the protection of natural persons with regard to the processing of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 1(3) the restriction or prohibition of the free movement of personal data within the Union for reasons connected with data protection is barred` MEANS
    IF `the personal data move within the Union`
       AND `the measure restricts or prohibits that movement`
       AND `the reason for the measure is connected with the protection of natural persons with regard to the processing of personal data`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- JUST TRUE is the text's own no to the measure, a flat negative: "shall be neither restricted nor prohibited for reasons connected with the protection of natural persons with regard to the processing of personal data".
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text names no party who restricts or prohibits, so no regulative rule is written (fork FK1-1); the provision bars a restriction or prohibition of the free movement "within the Union" and "for reasons connected with the protection of natural persons"; a movement outside the Union, a case with no measure, and a measure for another reason are outside it, and the text does not say whether such a measure is allowed.
